.Dd November 23, 2026
.Dt XTC_VERSION_STRING 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm xtc_version_string
.Nd return the xtc release name
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In xtc.h
.Ft const char *
.Fn xtc_version_string "void"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn xtc_version_string
function returns the name of the xtc release as a NUL-terminated string.
The returned pointer is to static storage and must not be freed.
.Pp
libxtc has two kinds of release.
A long-term-support release, from the
.Li lts/2.1
branch, is named by its ABI level in
.Em SemVer 2.0
format
.Pq Dq major.minor.patch , for example Dq 2.1.6 ,
and the string begins with the same numeric components that
.Xr xtc_version_components 3
reports.
A development release, from
.Li main ,
is named by its date in CalVer format
.Pq Dq YYYY.MM.DD , or Dq YYYY.MM.DD.N No for a second release on one day ,
for example
.Dq 2026.11.24 .
Its ABI level is not in the string; ask
.Xr xtc_version_components 3 ,
which says, for example, 2.3.0.
A tree that is neither, built from a checkout, is named by its ABI
level.
Both forms are checked by
.Pa test/m0/test_version.c .
.Pp
The same version is available at compile time as the
.Dv XTC_VERSION_STRING
macro
.Pq the release name
and the
.Dv XTC_VERSION_MAJOR ,
.Dv XTC_VERSION_MINOR
and
.Dv XTC_VERSION_PATCH
macros
.Pq the ABI level
of
.In xtc_version.h ,
which
.In xtc.h
includes.
That header, generated by the build and installed with the others,
also defines one
.Dv XTC_TLS_BACKEND_*
macro
.Pq Dv OPENSSL , MBEDTLS , GNUTLS , WOLFSSL , SCHANNEL No or Dv NONE ,
one
.Dv XTC_IO_BACKEND_*
macro
.Pq Dv URING , EPOLL , KQUEUE , POLL , SELECT , IOCP , SOLARIS , AIX No or Dv SIM ,
and
.Dv XTC_HAVE_UCONTEXT
when the platform has
.Xr swapcontext 3 .
A consumer compiled against one release and run against another sees
the compile-time macros of the first and the run-time string of the
second.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
A non-NULL pointer to a NUL-terminated string.
The string contents are stable for the lifetime of the process and
across all calls.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
#include <stdio.h>
#include <xtc.h>

int main(void) {
        printf("xtc %s\en", xtc_version_string());
        return 0;
}
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr xtc 7 ,
.Xr xtc_version_components 3 ,
.Xr xtc_strerror 3
.Sh STANDARDS
An LTS release name conforms to
.Lk https://semver.org SemVer 2.0 ;
a development release name is a CalVer date.
.Sh HISTORY
First appeared in xtc 0.0.1.
